efrin [1]. To the north of the Bell, the land drops off to a terrace 72 metres above sea level, which is where the Anglo-Saxon settlement was located [1]. In the early medieval period, the area was home to Gefrin (Yeavering), a Royal settlement in the Anglo-Saxon ruled kingdom of Bernicia [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95285", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95286", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144697", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Yeavering_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1381782.jpg/400px-Yeavering_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1381782.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/24f1c052/Old Yeavering 20140525.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235625", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235626", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''501''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:418481", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-12_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:418482", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-12_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''501'' -> ''-3500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('36d0cdd3-3586-46c5-bf1e-8cb4a70e1f6c'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-12-rollback:36d0cdd3-3586-46c5-bf1e-8cb4a70e1f6c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-12: mystery ''8'' restored on Moorgate', '168f35b8d6a4c5917a308d89bb5fbd77', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Gate/archway/bridge'', ''1000 - 1500 AD'') is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 3433e767f34031a8 (2026-11-12 10:36:17.26111+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 103 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07d''s own export (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82778", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2071:chunk-0001: description \"Moorgate was the last gate added to London''s defensive wall, originally a small postern that became a full gate in 1415 under Lord Mayor Thomas Falconer. Unlike the city''s other six gates, it was medieval rather than Roman in origin, providing access to the marshy Moorfields north of the wall. Enlarged in 1472 and 1511, then rebuilt in 1673 to become the grandest of London''s gates, it was demolished in 1761 with its stone reused to widen London Bridge.\" -> \"Moorgate was one of the City of London''s northern gates in its defensive wall, the last to be built [1]. The gate was demolished in 1762, but gave its name to a major street, Moorgate [1]. The earliest descriptions of Moorgate date from the early 15th century, where it was described as only a postern in the London city wall [1]. Located between Bishopsgate and Cripplegate and leading to a marshy open space known as Moorfields, it was not one of the larger or more important of the city gates [1]. In 1415 an ordinance enacted that the old postern be demolished [1]. It was replaced with a newer and larger structure located farther to the west, which included a wooden gate to be shut at night [1]. This gate was enlarged again in 1472 and 1511, and then damaged in the Great Fire of London in 1666 [1]. Although the City gates had ceased to have any modern function apart from decoration, it was replaced along with Ludgate, Newgate, and Temple Bar with a stone gate in 1672 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97184", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97185", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> ''1415''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146971", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/MoorHouse.jpg/400px-MoorHouse.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/36d0cdd3/Moorgate_Hollar.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
