    ('56876b69-7222-4afd-8204-5f1f00bd0725'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-12-rollback:56876b69-7222-4afd-8204-5f1f00bd0725:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-12: mystery ''9'' restored on Mandbjerghøj', '3b5d25018a75214c32bb1d040e151b90', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Petroglyphs'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 3 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 3433e767f34031a8 (2026-11-12 10:36:17.26111+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 103 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07d''s own export (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29448", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0289:chunk-0001: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30406", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84608", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2091:chunk-0001: description \"Mandbjerghoj is a Bronze Age petroglyph site located next to the road through Oster Velling Skov forest, north of Oster Velling, west of Randers in Jutland, Denmark. The site features two small granite boulders with engraved geometric patterns from the Bronze Age, positioned about 50 metres from their original find spot. A granite Fredningssten (heritage marker stone) marks the location. The nearly destroyed remains of the Mandbjerghoj tumulus, where the stones were originally found, lie nearby. The carvings are part of Denmark''s broader tradition of Bronze Age rock art featuring cup marks, spirals, and geometric designs.\" -> ''The Mandbjerghøj is located next to the road through Øster Velling Skov forest, north of Øster Velling, west of Randers in Jutland [1]. Here there are two small granite boulders with engraved geometric patterns from the Bronze Age [1]. The two stones with petroglyphs stand some fifty metres from their original find spot [1]. There are also the almost completely destroyed remains of the Mandbjerghøj tumulus where the first stone with petroglyphs, which was part of the tumulus fence, was found in 1857 [1]. The tumulus which is now barely visible was originally about 24 m in diameter and four metres high [1]. In the middle of the mound was a typical male grave of the early Bronze Age (c. 1500 BC) [1]. In the grave a bronze sword and a gilt belt-hook were found, which bore the same motif as the rock carvings, thereby demonstrating that the tumulus and the carvings were made at the same date [1]. The stones depict concentric rings and three ovals, which themselves enclose two rings [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150162", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/56876b69/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333826", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/56876b69/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
