rbian Grand Principality, in Novi Pazar. Founded in the 4th century during Roman rule, the structure features massive stone columns and an octagonal tower with an inner dome reflecting early Christian mausoleum architecture. Excavations beneath the floor unearthed Greek sculptures and black-figure pottery from the 7th-6th centuries BC, and a 5th-century BC princely grave with gold-silver jewellery. Stefan Nemanja, founder of the Nemanjic dynasty, was baptised here, symbolically marking the spiritual birth of the medieval Serbian state. It is part of the UNESCO World Heritage Site Stari Ras and Sopocani, inscribed in 1979.'' -> ''The Church of the Holy Apostles Peter and Paul (Petrova Crkva) is the oldest intact church in Serbia, situated on a hill of Ras, the medieval capital of the Serbian Grand Principality, in Novi Pazar [1]. Excavations beneath the floor unearthed Greek sculptures and black-figure pottery from the 7th-6th centuries BC, and a 5th-century BC princely grave with gold-silver jewellery [1] [2]. Stefan Nemanja, founder of the Nemanjic dynasty, was baptised here [1] [3]. It is part of the UNESCO World Heritage Site Stari Ras and Sopocani, inscribed in 1979 [1] [4] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:418483", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-12_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:418484", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-12_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''820'' -> ''-500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('658c8147-803d-4fa5-a335-bd1fe3573a28'::uuid, 'antiquity', '4', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-12-rollback:658c8147-803d-4fa5-a335-bd1fe3573a28:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-12: antiquity ''2'' restored on Sant''Agnello Maggiore', '3afc17e4a8fa312a4837cf325377ad78', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 4 from period_start -400"}, {"source": "production export 3433e767f34031a8 (2026-11-12 10:36:17.26111+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 103 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07d''s own export (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29350", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0276:chunk-0001: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Church/cathedral''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85012", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2102:chunk-0001: description \"Sant''Agnello Maggiore, also called Sant''Aniello a Caponapoli, is a church in the historical centre of Naples built above the ancient Greek double curtain city walls of Neapolis dating to the 4th century BC. Excavations from 1979 revealed sections of these Greek fortifications and 2nd-century AD Roman walls within the nave, now visible through protective glass walkways. Located at the highest point of the ancient city, the church is traditionally the burial site of Saint Agnello, the 6th-century bishop and co-patron of Naples. Severely bombed in 1943, the church was left in ruins for decades before restoration by the Superintendency and collaborative reopening by the Archiepiscopal Curia and Legambiente Campania. The marble high altar by Girolamo Santacroce (c.1524) survived the destruction.\" -> \"Sant''Agnello Maggiore, also called Sant''Aniello a Caponapoli or Santa Maria Intercede, is a church in the historical center of Naples [1]. Excavations starting in 1979 showed that the church was built above the ancient Greek (4th c. BC) double curtain city walls, now visible in the transept of the church, with interconnected braces and continuing outside in Largo Sant''Aniello [1]. 3rd century BC reinforcements to the walls are in the nave [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100829", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100830", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151722", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Resti_antichiNa.jpg'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/658c8147/Chiesa di Sant''Agnello Maggiore WLM25 003.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238563", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238564", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''501''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312069", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/658c8147/Chiesa di Sant''Agnello Maggiore WLM25 003.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/658c8147/Resti_antichiNa.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:418485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-12_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:418486", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-12_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''501'' -> ''-400''"}]'::jsonb),
