    ('c0319301-7c5f-42bc-9af0-808880e776c2'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-12-rollback:c0319301-7c5f-42bc-9af0-808880e776c2:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-12: mystery ''8'' restored on Grasburg, Rottleberode', '64a85213855bc7d105ecde7951732dc1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Castle/palace'', ''500 - 1000 AD'') is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 3433e767f34031a8 (2026-11-12 10:36:17.26111+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 103 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07d''s own export (2026-11-07 15:22:34.233295+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87206", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2164:chunk-0001: description \"A prehistoric refuge castle in the form of a hillfort with a rampart and ditch system, located in the Alter Stolberg woodland between Stempeda and Rottleberode in the South Harz region of Saxony-Anhalt, Germany. According to legend, it was the family seat of the Counts of Stolberg. In the 13th century a pilgrimage chapel was built in the castle grounds, where an annual fair was held until the 15th century, with a ceremony on St. Stephen''s Day recorded in 1497.\" -> \"The Grasburg is a prehistoric refuge castle, in the form of a hillfort with a rampart and ditch system [1]. The Grasburg is located in the wooded area known as Alter Stolberg between Stempeda and Rottleberode in the South Harz and is, according to legend, the family seat of the counts of Stolberg [1]. In the 13th century a pilgrimage chapel was built in the castle grounds, in which an annual fair was celebrated up to the 15th century [1]. Such a ceremony was held on St. Stephen''s Day (3 August) in 1497 on the Craßburg [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107880", "url": "